!!id:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/32/app/orders-errors-1.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/core.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/32/ltr8/http/problem-4.tn"
@doc:"""
  This service's business errors: the request was schema-valid, and the domain still said no.

  sku_not_found composes problem (§5.8), so it carries RFC 9457's members and adds its own. A record
  is closed under its type (§7.2), so the extension is declared rather than assumed -- which is what
  RFC 9457 does with an open JSON object, made explicit.

  Both imports are named. text would arrive through problem-4.tn's own import of core.tn either way,
  since imports are transitive, but a schema that uses a name should say where it comes from.
  Naming both was rejected until UPSTREAM.md #11 was fixed.
  """
{
  sku_not_found => problem & { missing_sku: non_empty_text }
}
